{∘})}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-{225}^{∘}) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-{225}^{∘}) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(-{225}^{∘}) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(-{225}^{∘})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image ${v}^{′}$ under the action of the matrix ${R}_{(-{225}^{∘})}$, we compute the matrix product, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}^{′} & ={R}_{(-{225}^{∘})}\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ -\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image is ${v}^{′}=⟨3\\sqrt{2},-\\sqrt{2}⟩.$" 13194139535957 true] [17592186376571 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376572 13194139535957 true] [17592186376571 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535957 true] [17592186376571 1041 "field-1" 13194139535957 true] [17592186376571 1104 #edb/ref 17592186376572 13194139535957 true] [17592186376571 1110 #uuid "2249e823-78df-55d1-9bbf-6f161f32c319" 13194139535957 true] [17592186376572 1034 "3\\sqrt{2}" 13194139535957 true] [17592186376572 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535957 true] [17592186376572 1111 #uuid "d47c04a9-561f-5a0e-9ec2-ed3c493396cb" 13194139535957 true] [17592186376573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376574 13194139535957 true] [17592186376573 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535957 true] [17592186376573 1041 "field-2" 13194139535957 true] [17592186376573 1104 #edb/ref 17592186376574 13194139535957 true] [17592186376573 1110 #uuid "81a98fac-9a0c-5216-9d36-b078269dc964" 13194139535957 true] [17592186376574 1034 "-\\sqrt{2}" 13194139535957 true] [17592186376574 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535957 true] [17592186376574 1111 #uuid "cff6832f-08f3-5294-a0bf-4fc631584b80" 13194139535957 true] [17592186376575 1017 #edb/ref 17592186376576 13194139535957 true] [17592186376575 1089 "q-8462" 13194139535957 true] [17592186376575 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535957 true] [17592186376575 1100 "What is the geometrical interpretation of the transformation represented by the matrix $A$ given below? \n\n \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535957 true] [17592186376575 1113 #uuid "29bbf036-1652-5f64-8437-aab9ecbcce39" 13194139535957 true] [17592186376575 1145 "The rotation matrix ${R}_{\\theta }$ represents a rotation of angle $\\theta $ counterclockwise about the origin and is given by\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nComparing $A$ with the rotation matrix, we have \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta <0$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta >0$ we must have $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi .$ \n\nDividing the first equation by the second gives\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =-1.\n$$\n\nThe principal value $\\theta $ is\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-1)=-\\frac{\\pi }{4},\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A$ represents a rotation of $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ radians *clockwise* about the origin." 13194139535957 true] [17592186376576 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376577 13194139535957 true] [17592186376576 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376578 13194139535957 true] [17592186376576 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376579 13194139535957 true] [17592186376576 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376580 13194139535957 true] [17592186376576 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376581 13194139535957 true] [17592186376576 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535957 true] [17592186376576 1041 "selection" 13194139535957 true] [17592186376576 1104 #edb/ref 17592186376577 13194139535957 true